From 7f0de687f2b9d54bc577edf01027f850453b8ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lolipuru <banstellazz@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:57:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] softisp: Add halo-free sharpening to the second pass

Sharpen luma in the denoise pass with an unsharp mask against a Gaussian
blur of the same 5x5 taps. Detail below a threshold is cored away so the
noise left after denoising isn't amplified, and the result is held within
the 3x3 neighbourhood's luma range plus a small margin, so edges get no
halos. The pass now also runs when only sharpening is on.

A Sharpen IPA algorithm sets the amount from a piecewise-linear table over
analogue gain (less at high gain) plus a fixed threshold.

On the S5K4H7 front camera at 16x gain, amount 1.0: 29% stronger edges
for 15% more luma noise, no visible halos.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: lolipuru <banstellazz@gmail.com>
